# Ponytail (Lean)

Minimize unrelated changes without sacrificing correctness or a coherent implementation; approved refactors are exempt from churn. Rationale comments ok, no noise. `stop.sh` advises on churn and mass reindent; it is advisory, not a block.

## Ladder
Prefer, when equally suitable, the lowest sufficient rung. Choose for correctness, clarity, and fit — not line count.
1. No implementation change (config, delete, existing API)
2. Existing repository code (Grep)
3. Stdlib / platform APIs
4. Installed dependencies (new dependency needs justification)
5. Small clear local implementation (not golfed)

## Size
Soft ~80 lines is a preference for focused modules. Split before 120 is a review prompt — do not split solely to meet a count. New hand-written files: hard 300; never 500. Legacy >700: localized fixes allowed without unrelated restructuring; new modules extracted ≤300. Generated, vendor, lockfiles, migrations, and declarative config are excluded. Scope is the total size of files you create or touch, not changed-line count.

## Quality
Match 1–2 siblings before Write. Named exports by default (framework-required default exports win). Early return. Nesting ≤2 as guidance; readability wins over clever flattening. Types per `types.mdc`; complexity per `complexity.mdc`. Remove dead code the task introduced or obsoleted. On a third occurrence, consider extraction when the instances share responsibility. Cleanup is limited to the task.

## Tools
`Read`, `Grep`, `Glob`, `Write`, `StrReplace` for hand-written changes. Shell for builds, tests, git, and approved validation/generation. Do not use Shell text rewriting (redirects, `sed`, `tee`); `before_shell.sh` denies it.

## Split
Over roof: Write new modules, `StrReplace` the original to imports, `Grep` callers. Never Shell `sed`.

## Verify
Run relevant tests, lint, and type checks when available. Review the final diff for unintended changes. Report checks not run and remaining uncertainty. Details in `testing.mdc`.

## Procedure
For a multi-file split, new module boundaries, or trade-offs, read the ponytail skill (`shared/skills/ponytail/SKILL.md`). If unavailable, follow this rule + repo conventions and report.
